      "question": "What drum kit did Dave Lombardo use on Seasons in the Abyss?",
      "answer": "Dave Lombardo used a Pearl Masters Custom kit for Seasons in the Abyss (1990), switching from the Tama Artstar II he had used on Reign in Blood (1986) and South of Heaven (1988). The Pearl Masters Custom featured maple shells — warmer and more open than the Tama's birch — with ISS tom mounting for improved resonance. The configuration included two 22-inch bass drums (not a double pedal), 10-inch and 12-inch rack toms, and 14-inch and 16-inch floor toms. This gear change is the most significant equipment transition between any two consecutive Rick Rubin Slayer productions."
